Once upon a time, before the time of Gods and heroes, there was a tribe. The Invi.
The Invi were invisible and could not interact with he visible world. They were the first expression of the Universe at creation.
They simply passed through the world, feeling bored most of the time since they couldn't do much. They loved to talk though and pass time together.
The Universe saw that and decided to help them, with a devious condition, as the Universe usually does.
It created the Aena. A tribe of people who could interact with the seen world just fine but could not see the unseen at all.
The trick was, that the Aena had a perfect Invi match. They two just had to find each other in a vast world and learn to love one another by finding some way to interact.
The result of a pair meeting each other, if their sould was pure, was to become Gods. Infinite power was given by the universe for a couple such as this.
Our main character is Vima, an Invi with a never ending desire to interact with the seen world, without knowing the tremendous power she could
get by meeting her Aena. She would be the first Invi to achieve this anyway.
One day, after helping with the chores of the village, she had to go bathe in the nearby lake. And there she saw him. An Aena as beautiful as light and
as kind as flowers. He was feeding a deer near the lake.
Desperately, she started thinking how she could interact with him. She thought and thought and thought and finally she found the way!
She ran back to the village and grabbed an Invi mirror. Invi mirrors were the only things that could interact with the sunlight.
She went back to the lake and, as the Aena was finishing feeding the deer, she held the mirror so the light went straight into his eyes.
He was blinded at first but after a while he noticed that the reflection came from a place that it should be possible.
He realized an Invi was trying to communicate.
He said "Ok, please light the lake. If I see a light at the water's surfece that means 'Yes', otherwise it means 'No'.
They started having endless conversation based on these two simple answers.
This went on for days until one day the Aena asked "What do you desire most in this world? Tell me and I'll bring it."
Then he started guessing. After many days of doing this and not seeing any light on the lake he started questioning if the Invi was still there.
He finally said "The Sun" to which he saw a light reflected on the lake. He paused. "How can I bring you the Sun?".
After he went back home that day he thought and thought and thought. He did not sleep that day in thought.
The next morning he rushed to the lake. He said "Here, the Sun for you at any place and any time" and he placed a sunflower in the lake.
Ripples of water appeared on its surface and as the light from the reflection of Vima's mirror reflected on them, light flew everywhere.
" I love you" Sym said and he kissed the sunflower.
Suddenly, he saw Vima in the morning light. Gorgeous and serene. She didn't realize he could see her so she kept reflecting at the lake.
He rose and headed towards her. Their kiss was the sweetest thing she'd ever tasted.
As they fell their powers rise beyond the mortal realm, the closed their eyes and let Love fill them with its infinite wisdom.
